Package: nirs4all
Type: Package
Title: Composable Near-Infrared Spectroscopy Pipelines for R
Version: 0.4.0.9019
Authors@R: c(person("Gregory", "Beurier", email = "gregory.beurier@cirad.fr", role = c("aut", "cre")), person("nirs4all", "contributors", role = "ctb"))
Description: Provides an R-facing pipeline API for near-infrared spectroscopy.
    Composes portable preprocessing (including local and robust normalization,
    area normalization, detrending, train-fitted MSC and Savitzky-Golay filtering) and partial
    least squares operations from 'n4m' with explicit R learner controllers,
    including optional 'parsnip' and 'mlr3' regression and classification
    adapters and a 'ranger' probability-forest classification controller.
    This development version offers
    local fit, predict, portable 'n4m' model serialization, and a native
    'dagml' cross-validation, fixed-candidate selection, refit and replay path
    for single-node pipelines and optional sequential n4m transform nodes,
    including fixed-candidate selection and parallel preprocessing branches
    joined before a model.
    Persisted refit models and transform states can predict new R samples.
    Optional 'nirs4allformats' datasets feed local and native paths with
    numeric or categorical targets while preserving sample and spectral-axis
    identities. Branching DAGs and host
    hyperparameter search remain under development.
